-- Test description
-- This test is intended to cover  multibuffer frames with collisions 
-- occurring at the beginning and end of varying length buffers. This will 
-- test the ability of the transmit buffer management to recover from these 
-- collisions and re-read the original start of the frame and try again.
--
-- Functional Coverage
-- · Ensures the functionality of the transmit buffers works properly.
-- · Ensures that the GEM responds properly to collisions during the 
--   transmission of multibuffer frames.
-- · Ensures the correct recovery of buffers that have had a collision 
--   detected during buffer activity.
--
-- Detailed test description
-- 1. Initialise GEM for 10 or 100 mode opeation.
-- Note: All transmit buffer descriptors in this test has bit 16 set in 
-- word zero. (No crc and padding to be added)
--
-- Frame One:  multibuffer frame- 5 buffers in total
-- 2. Transmit the first buffer (32 bytes) of the multibuffer frame.  
--    However, a collision is detected.  Therefore, a 32 bit jam 
--    sequence should be transmitted.
-- 3. Re-transmit the first buffer. However, a collision is detected.  
--    Therefore, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 4. Re-transmit the first buffer. Then, start transmitting the second 
--    buffer (16 bytes).  However, a collision is detected. 
--    Therefore, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 5. Re-transmit the first and second buffers. Then, transmit 
--    the third buffer (32 bytes) and the fourth buffer of (16 bytes). 
--    Finally, start to transmit the fifth buffer (8 bytes). 
--    However, a collision is detected. Therefore, a 32 bit jam 
--    sequence should be transmitted.
-- 6. Re-transmit all five frames correctly.
-- 7. Check status and statistics registers and ensure the above 
--     operations where handled properly.
--
-- Frame Two: multibuffer frame- 4 buffers in total
-- 8. Transmit the first buffer (8 bytes) and second buffer (8 byte) of
--    the multibuffer frame.  Then, start transmitting the third buffer 
--    (8 bytes) of the multibuffer frame.  However, a collision is 
--    detected (collision occurs during transmission of SFD with 
--    respect to the GEM).  Therefore, preamble and SFD should be 
--    completely transmitted. Then, a 32 bit jam sequence should be 
--    transmitted.
-- 9. Re-transmit the first three buffers. Then, start transmitting the 
--    last buffer (8 bytes).  However, a collision is detected.  
--    Therefore, a 32 bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 10. Re-transmit all four buffers correctly.
-- 11. Check status and statistics registers and ensure the 
--     above operations where handled properly.
--
-- Frame Three: multibuffer frame - 4 buffers in total
-- 12. Transmit four 1-byte frames. Then start transmitting another
--     1-byte frame.  However, a collision occurs during preamble. 
--     Check collision during preamble cause the GEM to transmit all 
--     of preamble , SFD and then a 32 bit jam sequence and the crc.
-- 13. Retry transmitting four 1-byte frames. Then start transmitting 
--     another 1-byte frame.  However, a collision occurs during preamble.  
--     Check collision during crc cause the GEM to transmit all of preamble, 
--     SFD and then a 32 bit jam sequence and the crc.
-- 14. Retry transmitting four 1-byte frames. Then start transmitting 
--     another 1-byte frame.  Check preamble, pad and crc are appended,
--     good frame sixty four bytes long, four bytes data
-- 15. Check status and statistics registers and ensure the above 
--     operations where handled properly.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ************************************************************************** --
-- 1. Initialize GEM
-- ************************************************************************** --
wait_states 4
bus_grant_delay 4

ten_meg_bit  -- 10Mbit/s operation (2.5Mhz tx_clk and rx_clk, 50MHz Pclk and Hclk)

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 --  check reset state

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      00 00000008  -- enable transmit
apbrd      00 00000008  -- check network control register
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbwr      04 00280000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      04 00280000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register



-- ************************************************************************** --
-- Setup a multi-buffer transmit queue in memory

apbwr      1c ffffff00  -- write address of transmit buffer descriptor in memory
apbrd      1c ffffff00  -- check transmit queue pointer
apbwr      00 00000208  -- Start the transmission by setting the go bit in network control register





